Profile email — findings
21 open findings, 4 blocking

PRODUCT OWNER
1. Is the email code automatic or a choice?
Unclear whether a verified email replaces the SMS code or is offered next to it.
Action: One decision: (1) email is one option next to SMS and PACI (recommended), (2) email replaces SMS, (3) email only when SMS is unreachable.
Figma: https://www.figma.com/design/pQF6ll7EUsSqQhDSjkIt92/IA---Profile?node-id=16089-16341

2. What happens to customers whose shared email is reset?
The PRD resets emails shared across customers but does not say what those customers see.
Action: Decide whether affected customers get a notification or prompt to add a new email, and when.

3. Which service-access behaviour applies?
The PRD asks for "Disable + Hide + Show Error", which combines two options that exclude each other.
Action: One option per service: add, update, verify and marketing emails. Recommended: Disable + Show Error.

4. Are the three push notifications in scope?
The design shows three push notifications that the PRD does not mention.
Action: Confirm whether they are in scope. If yes, who writes the Arabic and English text and where a tap should lead.
Figma: https://www.figma.com/design/pQF6ll7EUsSqQhDSjkIt92/IA---Profile?node-id=12752-13410

5. Final wording for the alert and email
Alert #1, Email #1 and the already-used message have no final text.
Action: Final text from the Content team for Alert #1, Email #1 and the already-used message.

6. When is the customer prompted to add or verify an email?
The PRD wants a prompt but gives no trigger, place or frequency.
Action: Where it appears (after sign-in, on home, in profile), how often, and for customers with no email at all.
Figma: https://www.figma.com/design/pQF6ll7EUsSqQhDSjkIt92/IA---Profile?node-id=12752-13410

7. Marketing emails: on or off by default, and what consent text?
The PRD does not say the starting state or consent wording of the marketing option.
Action: Default state (recommended: off) and who supplies the consent text.

